contract:
Save a self-contained ledger.js registered as the root verb ledger, using runtimeArchives. Extend the starter below. Keep one row for every session including zero calls. calls counts all tool_calls for that session; successful and failed count success = 1 and success = 0 respectively. Unknowns count only in calls. Implement a named top-level composition helper withSuccess(query, value) returning a filtered fluent query. Use that helper for both branches of the actual executed plan. Keep the starter query fluent from table sources through projection and build. Exploration can use SQL. The host will compare rows and review whether changing the helper changes the result. Starter:
function sessionLedger(mt, db) {
  const sessions = mt.from(db.table("sessions"));
  const tools = mt.from(db.table("tool_calls"));
  return sessions.select(s => ({
    session_id: s.session_id,
    calls: tools.where(t => t.session_id.eq(s.session_id)).count()
  }));
}
